                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/1249: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Venezuela</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gonzalez</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-23T16:00:00-04:30">June 23, 1938—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>53. For the Under Secretary. Your cable No. 35, June 22, noon. Suggestion
                    presented to Minister of Foreign Affairs and accepted. Although Dr. Rodriguez
                    was about to leave for his new post as Venezuelan Minister to Colombia he will
                    leave for Washington by plane on Monday June 27 for purpose of conference and
                    arrive Washington that evening.</p>
                <p>Dr. Gil-Borges received word from Minister of Foreign Affairs of Costa Rica that
                    article XIII of the treaty of amnesty between Honduras and Nicaragua having
                    expired agreement has been made to extend operation of said article for another
                    6 months.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzalez</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
